{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--ainu-classified-as-language-isolate","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--isolate"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu is classified as a language isolate with no demonstrated genetic relationship to any other known language family.","ja":"アイヌ語は他のいかなる語族とも系統的関係が立証されておらず、孤立言語として分類される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:janhunen2022@handbook-epub/l0010-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0069-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0074-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0025-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0011-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--coastal-relict-lineage-northern-eurasia","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--isolate"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu is one of four coastal language families in Northeast Asia and northern Eurasia that survive from before the post-Neolithic spreads of Inner Asian language families.","ja":"アイヌ語は、ポスト新石器時代の内陸アジア型語族の拡散以前から生き残った、北東アジア・北ユーラシアにおける4つの沿岸部言語系統の1つである。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0038-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0008-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--patrie-s-1982-proposal-connecting-ainu-to-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--altaic"],"statement":{"en":"Patrie's (1982) proposal connecting Ainu to the 'Altaic family'—grouping Ainu, Japanese, and Korean together with Turkic, Mongolic, and Tungusic—is extremely improbable, and its claimed sound correspondences are arbitrary and unconvincing.","ja":"パトリー（1982）によるアイヌ語・アルタイ語族同系説は、日本語と朝鮮語も加えたものであるが、成立する蓋然性は非常に低く、音韻対応づけも恣意的で説得力がない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0071-02","stance":"rejects"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--the-ainuic-kurilic-family-comprises-three-separate-languages","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--ethnogenesis"],"statement":{"en":"The Ainuic (Kurilic) family comprises three separate languages, corresponding to Hokkaido Ainu, Sakhalin Ainu, and Northern Kuriles Ainu.","ja":"アイヌ語族（千島語族）は、北海道アイヌ語、樺太アイヌ語、北千島アイヌ語という3つの個別言語から構成される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu","doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin","doculect:kuril/north"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:janhunen2022@handbook-epub/l0010-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--linguistic-evidence-points-to-an-origin-of-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--ethnogenesis"],"statement":{"en":"Linguistic evidence points to an origin of the Ainu language on the Asiatic mainland.","ja":"言語学的証拠は、アイヌの起源がアジア大陸にあることを示唆している。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0044-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--chamberlain-1887-denied-the-genetic-relationship-between-ainu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--japonic"],"statement":{"en":"Chamberlain (1887) denied the genetic relationship between Ainu and Japanese on the basis of 15 points, but all of them concerned grammatical and morphological (typological) differences rather than phonological correspondences.","ja":"チェンバレン（1887）は15の項目をあげてアイヌ語と日本語の系統関係を否定したが、そこで問題にしているのは文法や形態論的な類型論的違いばかりで、音韻対応に関する項目はひとつもない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--from-the-standpoint-of-linguistic-orthodoxy-chamberlain-s","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--japonic"],"statement":{"en":"From the standpoint of linguistic orthodoxy, Chamberlain's argument cannot establish that there is no genetic relationship between Ainu and Japanese.","ja":"チェンバレンの議論によってアイヌ語と日本語の間に系統関係が無いとすることは、言語学的な常識から言えばできない。"},"type":"judgement","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--kindaichi-1937-concluded-that-ainu-and-japanese-ultimately","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--japonic"],"statement":{"en":"Kindaichi (1937) concluded that Ainu and Japanese ultimately had different origins, largely agreeing with Chamberlain.","ja":"金田一（1937）はチェンバレンの論考にほぼ同意し、アイヌ語と日本語は本源の違う言語だったということに帰着せざるを得ないという結論を述べた。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0073-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--to-this-day-no-linguist-specializing-in-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--japonic"],"statement":{"en":"To this day, no linguist specializing in the Ainu language actively argues that Ainu and Japanese are genetically related.","ja":"現在にいたるまで、アイヌ語を専門とする言語学者で、積極的にアイヌ語と日本語の同系説を主張している者はいない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"actual","conditions":["among linguists specializing in Ainu"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0073-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--hattori-1956-claimed-that-a-distant-genetic-relationship","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--japonic"],"statement":{"en":"Hattori (1956) claimed that a distant genetic relationship between Ainu and Japanese is probable, citing the root kur (in kur, niskur, kunne, ekurok) and seven lexical comparisons (kap, se-, mat, tek, an, ne~na-, poye).","ja":"服部（1956）はアイヌ語と日本語に遠い親族関係がある蓋然性があると述べ、語根kur（kur、niskur、kunne、ekurokなど）の日本語kurosi等との類似および7語（kap、se-、mat、tek、an、ne~na-、poye）の例を挙げた。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["kur","niskur","kunne","ekurok","kap","se-","mat","tek","an","ne","na-","poye"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0073-03","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--the-hypothesis-relating-ainu-to-the-indo-european","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--macro"],"statement":{"en":"The hypothesis relating Ainu to the Indo-European language family, initiated by Batchelor (1887) and championed by Naert (1958), relied on inadequate descriptive materials and arbitrary sound correspondences, and currently has no supporters.","ja":"バチェラー（1887）に始まりナエール（1958）が代表したアイヌ語と印欧語族との同系説は、当時の不十分な言語資料と恣意的な音韻対応認定に基づいており、現在では支持されていない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0071-01","stance":"rejects"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--the-genetic-origins-and-external-affinities-of-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--macro"],"statement":{"en":"The genetic origins and external affinities of the Ainu language remain controversial, with no scholarly consensus having been reached.","ja":"アイヌ語の系統的起源および系統的親縁関係の問題は議論が続いており、研究者の間でいかなる合意にも達していない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0048-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--languages-surrounding-ainu-in-the-russian-far-east","revision":1,"topic":"topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topics":["topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison","topic:sources/genetic-position-macro-comparison--nivkh"],"statement":{"en":"Languages surrounding Ainu in the Russian Far East and adjacent areas—including Nivkh, Itermen, and Yukaghir—are likewise language isolates.","ja":"樺太北部とアムール川流域のニヴフ語、カムチャッカ半島のイテリメン語、サハ共和国のユカギール語など、アイヌ語の周辺には孤立言語が集まっている。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0070-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-06-38-590Z","status":"grouped"}
